{"id":"a57ed68f4a891fa9","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-tarski-seidenberg.md","title":"Tarski–Seidenberg Projection Theorem","display":"df-tarski-seidenberg — Tarski–Seidenberg Projection Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-tarski-seidenberg","aliases":["58-df-tarski-seidenberg"],"display":"df-tarski-seidenberg — Tarski–Seidenberg Projection Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-semialgebraic-set]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-tarski-seidenberg"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-tarski-seidenberg</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-tarski-seidenberg — Tarski–Seidenberg Projection Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c36cc156fef49a61\" href=\"?note=c36cc156fef49a61\" title=\"58-df-semialgebraic-set\">58-df-semialgebraic-set</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R}\\in V\">\\(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R}\\in V\\)</span> are one fixed real-closed ordered-field structure and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m,n\\in\\omega\">\\(m,n\\in\\omega\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A\\subseteq R^{m+n}\">\\(A\\subseteq R^{m+n}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi:R^{m+n}\\to R^m\">\\(\\pi:R^{m+n}\\to R^m\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"J:m\\to m+n\">\\(J:m\\to m+n\\)</span> selects the first <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"m\">\\(m\\)</span> coordinates</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RealClosedStructure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{RealClosedStructure}_S\\)</span>, the five-place <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CoordinateProjection}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CoordinateProjection}_S\\)</span>, and the eight-place <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S\\)</span> are the structure-explicit predicates from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"c36cc156fef49a61\" href=\"?note=c36cc156fef49a61\" title=\"58-df-semialgebraic-set\">58-df-semialgebraic-set</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}seidenberg}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{RealClosedStructure}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R})\n\\land m,n\\in\\omega\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{CoordinateProjection}_S(\\pi,R,m+n,m,J)\n\\land\\forall i&lt;m\\;(J(i)=i)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S(A,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R},m+n)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\longrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S(\\pi[A],R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R},m).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n&amp;\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}seidenberg}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{RealClosedStructure}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R})\n\\land m,n\\in\\omega\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{CoordinateProjection}_S(\\pi,R,m+n,m,J)\n\\land\\forall i&lt;m\\;(J(i)=i)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S(A,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R},m+n)\\\\\n&amp;\\quad\\longrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S(\\pi[A],R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,&lt;_{R},m).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The ambient real-closed structure, both dimensions, and the selected coordinates are shared by premise and conclusion.  The former compatibility predicates could choose unrelated hidden field operations for the two semialgebraic sets.</li>\n<li>This is a closure theorem, not a definition of semialgebraicity; the legacy filename is retained for link stability.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-semialgebraic-set","status":"resolved","id":"c36cc156fef49a61","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-semialgebraic-set]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-semialgebraic-set","status":"resolved","id":"c36cc156fef49a61","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RealClosedStructure}_S$, the five-place $\\mathrm{CoordinateProjection}_S$, and the eight-place $\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S$ are the structure-explicit predicates from [[58-df-semialgebraic-set]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,<_{R}\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"m,n\\in\\omega","display":false},{"tex":"A\\subseteq R^{m+n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\pi:R^{m+n}\\to R^m","display":false},{"tex":"J:m\\to m+n","display":false},{"tex":"m","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RealClosedStructure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CoordinateProjection}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}tarski\\text{-}seidenberg}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{RealClosedStructure}_S(R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,<_{R})\n\\land m,n\\in\\omega\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\mathrm{CoordinateProjection}_S(\\pi,R,m+n,m,J)\n\\land\\forall i<m\\;(J(i)=i)\\\\\n&\\quad\\land\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S(A,R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,<_{R},m+n)\\\\\n&\\quad\\longrightarrow\n\\mathrm{Semialgebraic}_S(\\pi[A],R,+_R,\\cdot_R,0_R,1_R,<_{R},m).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true}],"bytes":1544,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1284","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-tarski-seidenberg.md|58-df-tarski-seidenberg]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["c36cc156fef49a61"]}